{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V13MemberIndicesa","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","roleHeading":"Type Alias","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"typealias","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L200","fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift"},"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" = ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V13MemberIndicesV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","text":"MemberIndices","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stored column of either plane, read in place: "},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/memberindices"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","role":"collection"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/memberindices","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stored column of either plane, read in place: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","kind":"symbol","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices ("},{"code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). No copy and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation, unlike a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged."}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices","kind":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a member of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The vertices are ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the columns,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hyperedges, are at positions ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" even when built from one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix","kind":"symbol","title":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}